The `if (percentileBlock.getValueCount(p) != 1)` check can be simplified. Since you are only interested in cases where the value count is greater than 1, you can directly use:
```java
if (percentileBlock.getValueCount(p) > 1) {
    warnings.registerException(new IllegalArgumentException("single-value function encountered multi-value"));
    result.appendNull();
    continue position;
}
```
This eliminates the unnecessary check for equality to 1 and makes the code cleaner.

